            "review_title": "Review at Sông - Seafood & Grill",
            "review_text": "manchesterianBangkok\nBangkok, Thailand\n534 contributions\n0\nDoubtful it's worth the drive\nJan 2024 • Couples\nIf your staying downtown in district 1 I would not recommend the 20 minute drive. Yes the seafood is very fresh as all kept in tanks but I'm sure you can find good seafood closer to home. The big surprise for me was that the hotel concierge made the booking for 7.15 and when we arrived the restaurant was empty and we were shown to the upper floor(metal staircase no handrails,you have been warned!) and sat at a table with a very limited view so attempted to move to a better table but was told all reserved. When we left 90 minutes later only 3 more customers! I was amazed by the prices as this is no fine dining establishment nor is it mentioned in the Michelin guide ,the cheapest fish was black grouper @ 790,000 dong per kilo( £26) plus service and taxes the smallest size was 1.25 kilo now £32 for a steamed fish seems very expensive for an out of the way restaurant in Saigon. On a positive note the spinach with garlic was only about £3\nRead more\nWritten January 2, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-05",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
